Rewritten: the Hermes plugin's one contribution — the transform_terminal_output
hook, which takes captured terminal output and answers it shorter, and leaves it
alone when the command failed, when the payload is too large, when the rewrite
would not be strictly shorter, or when anything goes wrong. That hook is here as
one :TOOL hook over Nodecode's eval and sh results, and the reduction the CLI
performed (ANSI stripping, adjacent dedupe, middle clamp, head/tail with an
omitted-line count, a minimum saving) is reimplemented in Common Lisp, together
with the /tokenjuice report the CLI's statistics give.

Left out: the tokenjuice CLI and its command-specific rule set (git, search,
install, network and the rest), its rule files and local configuration, its
artifact store, and the LangChain and FastMCP adapters, which the Hermes plugin
does not load either. The original consults the CLI for every call; this rewrite
holds no external process and no Node.js dependency, and folds every eligible
command with one general rule.
